Package: copeEH
Type: Package
Title: Coherent Population-Mortality-Adjusted Survival Extrapolation
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: person("Hao", "Chen", email = "hche2036@uni.sydney.edu.au",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fits jointly constrained marginal overall and progression-free
    survival curves using population mortality and transformed Bernstein
    relative-survival polynomials. Provides coherent health-state predictions,
    restricted state times, deterministic quality-adjusted life-years and
    state costs. Estimation uses a working-independence composite likelihood
    for separately available endpoint data. Patient-level dependence and
    transition hazards are not identified by this model.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: stats, graphics, utils
NeedsCompilation: no
LazyData: true
URL: https://github.com/haohaostats/copeEH
BugReports: https://github.com/haohaostats/copeEH/issues
